# Line endings: pinned only where CRLF actually breaks execution.
#
# These files are executed or parsed by Linux/POSIX tooling (shell, Docker,
# Docker Compose). A CRLF shell script dies with "\r: command not found" --
# an error message that explains nothing -- and a CRLF Dockerfile corrupts
# backslash line continuations and shell-form RUN/CMD. Pinning eol=lf makes
# the working-tree copy LF on every clone and checkout, independently of each
# developer's local core.autocrlf.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: a blanket `* text=auto`. It was considered and
# rejected (issue #40). Its first commit renormalizes every tracked file,
# which is a large diff that must be its own deliberate change, and for the
# rest of the repo the benefit is cosmetic. Do not "complete" this file by
# adding it -- reopen that decision first.

*.sh                 text eol=lf
Dockerfile*          text eol=lf
compose*.y*ml        text eol=lf
docker-compose*.y*ml text eol=lf
